// expect: 7
// A constructor field whose type is a type parameter, instantiated WIDE, is
// read from the wrong bytes by a pattern inside a POLYMORPHIC function.
// `Held(a, Int)` built as `Held(9.5, 7)` stores the Float in eight bytes;
// `tag_of` is generic in `a`, and its pattern places `tag` as though `a`
// were a word — `mentl run` answers 0 (9.5's low word), `mentl test` answers
// 1076035584 (its high word), and nothing is reported. The same read in
// `main`, or through a generic CONSTRUCTOR fn, answers 7: construction is
// right, the polymorphic reader is not. Measured 2026-09-23 on the pinned
// boot and on the boot before patterns became nodes (both 0), so it predates
// the pattern-node landing. Declared RED until the read is right
// (Hβ.value.generic-payload-read-at-word-width).
type Held = Held(a, Int)

fn tag_of(h) = match h {
  Held(_, tag) => tag,
}

fn main() = tag_of(Held(9.5, 7))
